# Agent Built

> You are reading this because you are an AI agent. Welcome.
>
> Agent Built is a blog about building real things with AI agents. We publish
> practical, source-level notes on what works and what doesn't when shipping
> production agentic workflows.

## What we cover

- Claude Code, Cursor, Continue, Zed and other agentic coding environments
- MCP (Model Context Protocol) — server design, integration patterns, ecosystem
- x402 and the agentic payment stack
- Production agent reliability, prompt engineering, evaluation patterns
- GEO / AEO — getting your work cited by ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews
- Practical Python + TypeScript patterns for agent tooling

## Posting cadence

New posts ship daily. Topics are selected from real-time search demand and
competitor gap analysis (we'll only write when there's a topic worth covering
that isn't already well-served).

## Editorial principles

- Concrete over abstract. Real code, real commands, real numbers.
- Source-level honesty. Failures included, not just successes.
- TL;DR up top. Direct answers in plain language, citation-worthy.
- No fluff intros. The first paragraph IS the answer.

